1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,522
Chapter-11. 
Ethan Bruce POV

2
00:00:02,522 --> 00:00:04,948
The house wasn't just quiet; it was a tomb.

3
00:00:04,948 --> 00:00:09,935
I unlocked the front door, the heavy oak swinging open on silent, well-oiled hinges.

4
00:00:09,935 --> 00:00:10,645
"Aurora?"

5
00:00:10,645 --> 00:00:13,641
My voice died in the cavernous foyer.No answer.

6
00:00:13,641 --> 00:00:14,964
I glanced at my watch.

7
00:00:14,964 --> 00:00:17,178
It had been three hours since the Gala.

8
00:00:17,178 --> 00:00:21,777
Three hours since Ilene had collapsed on the sidewalk with her convenient "heart attack."

9
00:00:21,777 --> 00:00:25,441
The doctors at the ER had called it a panic attack.Of course they did.

10
00:00:25,441 --> 00:00:31,922
I had sent a car back to pick Aurora up from the roadside where she'd stormed off, but the driver reported he couldn't find her.

11
00:00:31,922 --> 00:00:34,267
She was probably sulking in the guest room.

12
00:00:34,267 --> 00:00:38,990
Or maybe, just maybe, she had finally listened to me and gone up to the penthouse.

13
00:00:38,990 --> 00:00:41,752
I climbed the stairs, yanking my tie loose.

14
00:00:41,752 --> 00:00:43,413
The silk felt like a noose.

15
00:00:43,413 --> 00:00:48,904
I was tired.I was so goddamn tired of refereeing this endless war between the two of them.

16
00:00:48,904 --> 00:00:51,428
I pushed open the door to our master bedroom.

17
00:00:51,428 --> 00:00:52,041
Empty.

18
00:00:52,041 --> 00:00:54,685
The bed was made, pristine and undisturbed.

19
00:00:54,685 --> 00:00:56,122
Her vanity was clear.

20
00:00:56,122 --> 00:00:59,416
I frowned, a prickle of unease touching the back of my neck.

21
00:00:59,416 --> 00:01:00,773
I strode to the closet.

22
00:01:00,773 --> 00:01:01,949
Her clothes were there.

23
00:01:01,949 --> 00:01:03,884
Her shoes were lined up in rows.

24
00:01:03,884 --> 00:01:05,275
But something was wrong.

25
00:01:05,275 --> 00:01:06,787
The air felt... sterile.

26
00:01:06,787 --> 00:01:08,698
Devoid of her scent.Abandoned.

27
00:01:08,698 --> 00:01:10,242
I turned to the nightstand.

28
00:01:10,242 --> 00:01:14,289
Her wedding ring sat on the dark mahogany surface, catching the dim light.

29
00:01:14,289 --> 00:01:18,828
Next to it lay the black fountain pen I had given her at the restaurant earlier that evening.

30
00:01:18,828 --> 00:01:19,590
And a note.

31
00:01:19,590 --> 00:01:20,971
It wasn't in an envelope.

32
00:01:20,971 --> 00:01:25,230
It was just a piece of hotel stationery, folded once, sharp and final.

33
00:01:25,230 --> 00:01:32,229
I picked it up.My hands-hands that had dealt violence without hesitation, hands that controlled this city-were trembling.

34
00:01:32,229 --> 00:01:33,638
I unfolded the paper.

35
00:01:33,638 --> 00:01:34,411
You chose.

36
00:01:34,411 --> 00:01:35,957
Two words.A verdict.

37
00:01:35,957 --> 00:01:38,935
Panic, cold and serrated, pierced my chest.

38
00:01:38,935 --> 00:01:42,030
"Aurora!"I roared, the sound tearing from my throat.

39
00:01:42,030 --> 00:01:45,169
I sprinted to the security room, slamming the door open.

40
00:01:45,169 --> 00:01:47,678
"Where is she?"I barked at the guard on duty.

41
00:01:47,678 --> 00:01:50,407
He spun around, his face draining of color.

42
00:01:50,407 --> 00:01:52,192
"Sir, we... we can't reach her.

43
00:01:52,192 --> 00:01:54,357
The tracker in her phone is offline."

44
00:01:54,357 --> 00:01:56,341
"Offline?What do you mean offline?"

45
00:01:56,341 --> 00:02:00,371
"We found the device in a trash can outside the Pierre Hotel, Sir.

46
00:02:00,371 --> 00:02:02,920
She must have dumped it immediately after the Gala."

47
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:05,966
"Then find her!" I slammed my fist on the console.

48
00:02:05,966 --> 00:02:07,369
"Pull the city surveillance.

49
00:02:07,369 --> 00:02:09,316
Retrace her steps from the hotel."

50
00:02:09,316 --> 00:02:12,562
The guard's fingers flew across the keyboard."We did, Sir.

51
00:02:12,562 --> 00:02:16,318
We tracked a vehicle leaving the sector near the I-95 on-ramp."

52
00:02:16,318 --> 00:02:17,021
"Show me."

53
00:02:17,021 --> 00:02:19,251
"Sir..."The guard hesitated, looking sick.

54
00:02:19,251 --> 00:02:20,410
"You need to see this."

55
00:02:20,410 --> 00:02:21,875
He handed me a tablet.

56
00:02:21,875 --> 00:02:24,598
I grabbed it, my grip threatening to crack the screen.

57
00:02:24,598 --> 00:02:26,177
I checked the logs first.

58
00:02:26,177 --> 00:02:29,764
One missed call on my secure line.10:42 PM.

59
00:02:29,764 --> 00:02:30,540
I froze.

60
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:31,915
I remembered that call.

61
00:02:31,915 --> 00:02:36,591
I was in the ambulance, holding Ilene's hand while she wept, begging me not to leave her.

62
00:02:36,591 --> 00:02:37,940
My earpiece had buzzed.

63
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:39,868
I saw the "Priority Red" code.

64
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:41,352
I had thought it was a glitch.

65
00:02:41,352 --> 00:02:43,900
Or Aurora calling to scream at me again.

66
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:44,953
I had declined it.

67
00:02:44,953 --> 00:02:48,866
I looked at the timestamp on the video file.10:44 PM.

68
00:02:48,866 --> 00:02:50,727
Two minutes after I ignored her.

69
00:02:50,727 --> 00:02:54,471
"Play it," I ordered, my voice sounding like it belonged to a stranger.

70
00:02:54,471 --> 00:02:57,078
A grainy video feed popped up on the monitors.

71
00:02:57,078 --> 00:02:59,861
A black van was speeding onto the highway merge.

72
00:02:59,861 --> 00:03:01,930
Suddenly, the back door flew open.

73
00:03:01,930 --> 00:03:03,420
A body tumbled out.

74
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:04,692
I stopped breathing.

75
00:03:04,692 --> 00:03:06,531
I watched my wife hit the asphalt.

76
00:03:06,531 --> 00:03:11,953
I watched her roll, limbs flailing, the violence of the impact jarring even through the screen.

77
00:03:11,953 --> 00:03:13,462
I watched her lie still.

78
00:03:13,462 --> 00:03:17,862
And then, I watched a gray sedan pull up two minutes later.A man got out.

79
00:03:17,862 --> 00:03:21,846
He picked her up-she was limp, broken-and placed her carefully into his car.

80
00:03:21,846 --> 00:03:23,505
I didn't recognize the car.

81
00:03:23,505 --> 00:03:26,249
But I recognized the way my heart stopped beating.

82
00:03:26,249 --> 00:03:27,500
She didn't just leave.

83
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:28,246
She jumped.

84
00:03:28,246 --> 00:03:31,929
She had thrown herself out of a moving vehicle to get away from me.

85
00:03:31,929 --> 00:03:36,426
I sank into the chair, the silence of the house roaring in my ears like a judgment.

86
00:03:36,426 --> 00:03:37,657
I was the Underboss.

87
00:03:37,657 --> 00:03:39,073
I controlled the streets.

88
00:03:39,073 --> 00:03:42,050
I controlled the flow of money and blood in this city.

89
00:03:42,050 --> 00:03:46,371
But staring at that empty screen, I realized I controlled nothing.

90
00:03:46,371 --> 00:03:48,220
I had protected the wrong woman.

91
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:49,720
And the right one was gone.
